;. /grove_app_authoring_flow
  ;@ /flow/definition grove_app_authoring
  ;= Author a Grove application in the live namespace
    Bind sources to task, grove and authoring evidence; bind provider to the raw
    interactive provider record. The grove-authoring mount supplies native
    source draft actions and the existing compiler supplies preview and publish.
    A task names a draft, domain records, interactions and publication intent.
    The bundled task creates a small notes app in preview only.

    ;@ /flow/input sources
    ;= App brief and native Grove contracts
    ;@ /flow/input provider
    ;= Interactive provider

    ;@ /flow/step task ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/library/surface_task
    ;@ /flow/bind pages document
    ;@ /flow/bind sources sources
    ;= Prepare a scoped app authoring task

    ;@ /flow/step authored ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/interactive_requests
    ;@ /flow/bind tasks task
    ;@ /flow/bind provider provider
    ;= Use native draft actions and compiler diagnostics

    ;@ /flow/step report ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/library/report_pages
    ;@ /flow/bind responses authored
    ;= Read the validated authoring report

    ;@ /flow/step pages ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/evidence
    ;@ /flow/bind pages report
    ;@ /flow/bind sources sources
    ;= Retain source provenance with the report

    ;@ /flow/result pages
    ;= App authoring report

    ;@ /flow/page /
    ;@ /flow/uses task grove authoring
    ;= Grove application
      Read the task and reference syntax. Start with cohesive domain records,
      roles, typed slots, a useful view and the declared actions required by
      the task. Reuse installed codecs and native controls. Do not create a
      JavaScript state model, host compiler or alternate work queue.

      Discover Create and compile draft on the grove-authoring workspace. Its
      default-node receiver is /0x11/app/grove_authoring. Use the active node's
      actual address and discovered schema. Supply an unused name and complete
      Grove source. The native host fixes the preview and publication roots.
      Read the native job: revision, attempted, ready, published, message and
      line. Its status_path links an ordinary read-only cell projection of the
      same source and fields. Creation acceptance is not compilation success. A ready revision
      must equal the current revision before claiming a successful preview.

      Inspect the installed preview records and discover their Goo controls.
      Exercise only mutations authorized by the task, on preview samples.
      Read resulting records and receipts. Fix compile diagnostics by saving
      source against the current revision, then inspect again. Invalid source
      remains editable; an older successful preview is not the new result.

      Publish only if the task explicitly requests it, for the exact ready
      revision. Inspect the resulting published value and instance afterward.
      Publication replaces this draft's installed published sample instance;
      it is not a migration of a business's existing data. Do not point it at
      an existing production application. If the task asks for that, report
      the required explicit installation/adoption decision instead.

      On retry inspect retained action receipts and the draft before creating
      anything. Reuse a draft only when the original receipt or explicit task
      establishes ownership. Never overwrite someone else's draft. Ask through
      the existing input hole when domain requirements or authority are missing.
      Report exact draft, preview, publication and receipt addresses, the
      compiled revision and observed checks. A report alone proves none of them.
